# 32. SECURITY

Implement Supabase Row Level Security.

Admin users may:

* Manage master data
* Read feedback
* View analytics
* Generate reports

Public/student users may:

* Read only the active academic information required to populate the feedback form
* Submit valid feedback
* Submit associated ratings

Public users must NOT be able to:

* Read all feedback responses
* Read student comments
* Modify existing feedback
* Delete feedback
* Access admin data
* Access admin dashboard APIs

Do not expose the Supabase service-role key in frontend code.

Use only safe client-side environment variables in the browser.

---

# 33. DUPLICATE/SPAM PROTECTION

Design basic protection against repeated or automated submissions.

At minimum:

* Disable the submit button while submission is processing.
* Validate all values server-side/database-side where possible.
* Verify that selected course/faculty mapping is active.
* Add rate limiting or server-side submission protection for production deployment.

If the institution later wants “one feedback per student per course,” implement authenticated or token-based submission without exposing student identity in faculty reports.

Do not pretend browser localStorage alone provides secure duplicate prevention.

---

# 34. DATABASE TRANSACTION SAFETY

A feedback submission consists of:

1. Feedback parent record
2. 15 feedback rating records

Ensure partial submissions do not produce corrupted analytics.

Prefer a secure PostgreSQL function/RPC or backend endpoint that validates the request and inserts the feedback plus all ratings atomically in one transaction.

